WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.822
Container images should not contain production secrets.

2
00:00:03.822 --> 00:00:13.730
Secrets include connection strings, API keys, tokens, certificates, private keys, package feed credentials, signing keys, and cloud credentials.

3
00:00:13.730 --> 00:00:22.935
If a secret is baked into an image layer, it can spread through registries, caches, developer machines, build systems, and older image tags.

4
00:00:22.935 --> 00:00:30.502
Runtime configuration should be separated by environment and injected through controlled platform mechanisms.

5
00:00:30.502 --> 00:00:38.302
Development, staging, and production should not share secret material or accidentally override reviewed behavior.

6
00:00:38.302 --> 00:00:47.429
Local compose files, sample settings, and developer convenience configuration should not drift into production images or deployments.

7
00:00:47.429 --> 00:00:57.961
Environment variables can be useful for ordinary configuration, but sensitive values need access control, logging review, and platform-specific handling.

8
00:00:57.961 --> 00:01:10.442
Secret mounts, orchestrator secrets, managed identities, workload identities, and external secret stores can reduce secret sprawl when teams govern who can read them and how they rotate.

9
00:01:10.442 --> 00:01:14.577
ASP. NET Core configuration precedence should be understood.

10
00:01:14.577 --> 00:01:24.250
Values can come from files, environment variables, command line arguments, user secrets in development, mounted files, and platform providers.

11
00:01:24.250 --> 00:01:34.235
A later source may override an earlier reviewed setting, so teams should document expected sources and validate sensitive production configuration.

12
00:01:34.235 --> 00:01:38.213
Diagnostics and support workflows must not expose secrets.

13
00:01:38.213 --> 00:01:52.879
Logs, crash dumps, environment dumps, exception pages, health endpoints, screenshots, shell history, and support bundles can all reveal container environment values or mounted secret contents if they are not reviewed.

14
00:01:52.879 --> 00:01:57.716
Redaction should be designed into the application and platform process.
